  "notes": "CardDemo's main menu (transaction CM00), pseudo-conversational: first entry sends the menu; re-entered with an option it XCTLs to the option's program (option 11, the authorization module, only when INQUIRE PROGRAM finds it installed), or re-sends the menu with a message; PF3 returns to sign-on. Options 0 and 12 are rejected, and are then still used as a subscript of the 11-entry table (CDEMO-MENU-OPT-USRTYPE(WS-OPTION)) -- storage beside the table, not an error, in COBOL. Derived from CardDemo (Apache-2.0; Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): LICENSE and NOTICE here are the source's own."
